<h3 data-section-id=3D"1i4ixsx" data-start=3D"557" data-end=3D"584">Why one=
 sheet is better</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"585" data-end=3D"755">
<li data-section-id=3D"1922na1" data-start=3D"585" data-end=3D"636">
<p data-start=3D"587" data-end=3D"636">Easier for recruiters and interviewe=
rs to review.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"p9e0k5" data-start=3D"637" data-end=3D"672">
<p data-start=3D"639" data-end=3D"672">Looks organized and professional.</p=
>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1rxdrx" data-start=3D"673" data-end=3D"699">
<p data-start=3D"675" data-end=3D"699">Easier to link with RTM.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"kljcby" data-start=3D"700" data-end=3D"755">
<p data-start=3D"702" data-end=3D"755">Common practice in small and medium =
testing projects.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"757" data-end=3D"794">For your GitHub project, I'd suggest=
:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"796" data-end=3D"1033">
<li data-section-id=3D"1pkkg5b" data-start=3D"796" data-end=3D"859">
<p data-start=3D"798" data-end=3D"859"><strong data-start=3D"798" data-end=
=3D"816">TestCases.xlsx</strong> =E2=86=92 1 sheet containing all 15=E2=80=
=9320 test cases.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"yb38gs" data-start=3D"860" data-end=3D"920">
<p data-start=3D"862" data-end=3D"920"><strong data-start=3D"862" data-end=
=3D"884">TestScenarios.xlsx</strong> =E2=86=92 1 sheet containing all scena=
rios.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"ipjws7" data-start=3D"921" data-end=3D"972">
<p data-start=3D"923" data-end=3D"972"><strong data-start=3D"923" data-end=
=3D"941">BugReport.xlsx</strong> =E2=86=92 1 sheet containing all bugs.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"xff7y9" data-start=3D"973" data-end=3D"1033">
<p data-start=3D"975" data-end=3D"1033"><strong data-start=3D"975" data-end=
=3D"987">RTM.xlsx</strong> =E2=86=92 1 sheet containing the traceability ma=
trix.</p>
</li>
</ul>
